@startuml
title MODRISS Phase 3 — Interrupt-Driven Operations and Maintenance Pull Flow

skinparam backgroundColor #F5F3ED
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFBF7
  BorderColor #617178
  FontColor #102C3A
  DiamondBackgroundColor #D7E9E5
  DiamondBorderColor #087B78
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EBE8DF
  BorderColor #B4653C
}

start
repeat
  :Capture one production signal, incident, request,\nprovider event or improvement as WP-30;
  :Classify three independent axes:\nmaintenance purpose; emergency status; class of service;
  :Replenish from ready demand and pull only when\nWP-31 WIP limits and capacity permit;

  if (Emergency restoration required?) then (yes)
    :Restore service under expedite policy;
    :Keep every temporary change open until removed\nor reconciled with its authoritative source;
  else (no)
    :Execute the pulled item using its explicit policy;
  endif

  :Verify restoration or change evidence; update trace,\nage, cycle time, throughput and SLE observations;

  if (Accepted disposition?) then (operations-only)
    :Close WP-30 with operational evidence;\nno release is created;
  elseif (bounded shortest safe MDE/release path) then (bounded)
    :Route to the earliest authoritative source; propagate\nand obtain applicable release controls;
  else (planned release backlog)
    :Commit explicitly to a later release hypothesis;
  endif

repeat while (Service active and no release/retirement transition selected?) is (pull next item)
-> transition selected;

note right
  Maintenance purpose does not determine urgency.
  Emergency status does not determine class of service.
  Class of service does not determine engineering impact.
end note

stop
@enduml
